  "about": [
    "Year / make / model -> bolt pattern, for the Verified Fitment finder.",
    "",
    "SOURCE OF TRUTH. tools/build-bolts.js compiles this into vehicle-bolts.js",
    "for the browser. Edit this file, never that one.",
    "",
    "HOW TO READ AN ENTRY. `from`/`to` are inclusive model years. An entry ends",
    "where the pattern changes, not where the body style changes — the whole",
    "point is the generation break, so 2010 and 2011 GM HD are two rows and",
    "that is deliberate.",
    "",
    "`confidence` is honest, not decorative:",
    "  high   - a pattern I would stake a wheel order on; widely published and",
    "           consistent across sources.",
    "  check  - believed right, but the generation break or a trim split makes",
    "           it worth confirming against the customer's actual truck.",
    "Nothing here has been checked against a physical vehicle. Until someone",
    "does that, the UI must say the pattern is confirmed before the wheels are",
    "built, not that it fits. CLAUDE.md rule 1.",
    "",
    "THE TRAPS, which are why this file exists at all:",
    "  - Ford Super Duty is 8x170. GM HD is 8x180. Ram HD is 8x165.1. Three",
    "    different eight-lugs that look identical in a photograph.",
    "  - Ram 1500 Classic (2019-2024) is the OLD 5x139.7 truck wearing a new",
    "    year. The 2019+ DT next to it on the lot is 6x139.7. Same name, same",
    "    model year, wheels do not swap either way.",
    "  - GM 2500/3500HD changed 8x165.1 -> 8x180 for 2011.",
    "  - Toyota Tundra went 6x139.7 -> 5x150 for 2007 and back to 6x139.7 for",
    "    2022. Sequoia follows it one year later each way.",
    "  - Nissan Titan XD is 8x180 while the Titan beside it is 6x139.7.",
    "  - The F-450/F-550 pickup is a ten-lug on 225mm with 19.5in wheels. It is",
    "    not a wider F-350."
  ],
